lear long-term change (+0.93 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 63.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 1991 (102.37 in); the driest, 2000 (38.88 in). New Orleans almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}